        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The <strong>distributive law</strong> describes how multiplication works when it is applied to a sum inside parentheses.</p>",
            "readable_text": "The distributive law describes how multiplication works when it is applied to a sum inside parentheses.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>When a number is multiplied by a sum, the multiplication is <strong>distributed</strong> to each term in the sum. In other words, the number outside the parentheses multiplies every term inside the parentheses.</p>",
            "readable_text": "When a number is multiplied by a sum, the multiplication is distributed to each term in the sum. In other words, the number outside the parentheses multiplies every term inside the parentheses.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, consider the expression <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3(2x + 5).]</span> The number <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3]</span> multiplies both terms inside the parentheses:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, consider the expression [MATH: 3(2x + 5).] The number [MATH: 3] multiplies both terms inside the parentheses:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3(2x + 5)|=; 3 \u22c5 2x + 3 \u22c5 5|=; 6x + 15]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 3(2x + 5)|=; 3 \u22c5 2x + 3 \u22c5 5|=; 6x + 15]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>After applying the distributive law, the parentheses are removed, and the expression is written as a sum of the resulting terms.</p>",
            "readable_text": "After applying the distributive law, the parentheses are removed, and the expression is written as a sum of the resulting terms.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>In this lesson, you will learn how to apply the distributive law to different linear expressions.</p>",
            "readable_text": "In this lesson, you will learn how to apply the distributive law to different linear expressions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nThe distributive law describes how multiplication works when it is applied to a sum inside parentheses.\n\nContent:\nWhen a number is multiplied by a sum, the multiplication is distributed to each term in the sum. In other words, the number outside the parentheses multiplies every term inside the parentheses.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the expression [MATH: 3(2x + 5).] The number [MATH: 3] multiplies both terms inside the parentheses:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 3(2x + 5)|=; 3 \u22c5 2x + 3 \u22c5 5|=; 6x + 15]\n\nContent:\nAfter applying the distributive law, the parentheses are removed, and the expression is written as a sum of the resulting terms.\n\nContent:\nIn this lesson, you will learn how to apply the distributive law to different linear expressions."
      },
