    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law describes how multiplication works when it is applied to a sum inside parentheses.\n\nContent:\nWhen a number is multiplied by a sum, the multiplication is distributed to each term in the sum. In other words, the number outside the parentheses multiplies every term inside the parentheses.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the expression [MATH: 3(2x + 5).] The number [MATH: 3] multiplies both terms inside the parentheses:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 3(2x + 5)|=; 3 \u22c5 2x + 3 \u22c5 5|=; 6x + 15]\n\nContent:\nAfter applying the distributive law, the parentheses are removed, and the expression is written as a sum of the resulting terms.\n\nContent:\nIn this lesson, you will learn how to apply the distributive law to different linear expressions.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Number Over the Sum of Two Terms\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: (7 + 4y)\\cdot 6=]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 6\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: (7 + 4y) \u22c5 6|=; 7 \u22c5 6 + 4y \u22c5 6|=; 42 + 24y]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5(8x + 3) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 40x \u2212 15]\nb. [MATH: 40x + 8]\nc. [MATH: 13x + 8]\nd. [MATH: 40x \u2212 8]\ne. [MATH: 40x + 15]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3 + 6z) \u22c5 4 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 7 + 10z]\nb. [MATH: 12 + 24z]\nc. [MATH: 3 + 24z]\nd. [MATH: 1 + 2z]\ne. [MATH: 24 + 12z]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Number Over the Sum of Two Variable Terms\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: 4(3a + 7b)=]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 4\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 4(3a + 7b)|=; 4 \u22c5 3a + 4 \u22c5 7b|=; 12a + 28b]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 5(2k + 5m) =][FREE_ENTRY 1]\n[MATH: k +]\n[FREE_ENTRY 2]\n[MATH: m]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (2u + 5v) \u22c5 4 =][FREE_ENTRY 1]\n[MATH: u +]\n[FREE_ENTRY 2]\n[MATH: v]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Tutorial: Dealing With a Minus Inside the Parentheses\n\nContent:\nThe distributive law can also be used when the expression inside the parentheses is a difference.\n\nContent:\nWhen a number is multiplied by an expression with a minus sign, the number outside the parentheses still multiplies every term inside the parentheses. The subtraction sign stays between the terms.\n\nContent:\nFor example, consider the expression [MATH: 5(4x - 3).] The number [MATH: 5] multiplies both [MATH: 4x] and [MATH: 3.]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 5(4x \u2212 3)|=; 5 \u22c5 4x \u2212 5 \u22c5 3|=; 20x \u2212 15]\n\nContent:\nAfter distributing, the parentheses are removed, and the expression is written as the difference of the resulting terms.\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Number Over the Difference of Two Terms\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: (9x - 4)\\cdot 5=]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 5\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: (9x \u2212 4) \u22c5 5|=; 9x \u22c5 5 \u2212 4 \u22c5 5|=; 45x \u2212 20]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 7(5k \u2212 3) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 35k \u2212 4]\nb. [MATH: 7k \u2212 21]\nc. [MATH: 35k \u2212 21]\nd. [MATH: 35k \u2212 3]\ne. [MATH: 5k \u2212 3]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (4x \u2212 1) \u22c5 9 =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 24x \u2212 9]\nb. [MATH: 36x \u2212 4]\nc. [MATH: 4x \u2212 9]\nd. [MATH: 36x \u2212 1]\ne. [MATH: 36x \u2212 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Example: Distributing a Number Over the Difference of Two Variable Terms\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: 6(2p - 5q)=]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nUsing the distributive law, we multiply each term inside the parentheses by the number [MATH: 6\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 6(2p \u2212 5q)|=; 6 \u22c5 2p \u2212 6 \u22c5 5q|=; 12p \u2212 30q]\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 3(5u \u2212 v) =][FREE_ENTRY 1]\n[MATH: u \u2212]\n[FREE_ENTRY 2]\n[MATH: v]\n\n---\n\nItem 14 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (3w \u2212 7z) \u22c5 2 =][FREE_ENTRY 1]\n[MATH: w \u2212]\n[FREE_ENTRY 2]\n[MATH: z]"
